Theorem TF-3: Construct produces FRESH state

  Preconditions:
    - dst is defined by Construct(ctor) at program point p
    - shape_from_ctor maps ctor to its shape per Annex E §AIMS TF-3:
        Struct -> R<S>
        EnumVariant -> R<V>
        ListLiteral | SetLiteral | MapLiteral -> C
        Tuple | Closure -> Phi
    - TF is the forward transfer function per the canonical proof notation-canonical
      sec-Transfer-Function-Notation

  Soundness property:
    Forall ctor.
      TF(s, Construct(ctor))[dst]
        = FRESH(shape_from_ctor(ctor))
        = (O, L, 1, u, bl, shape_from_ctor(ctor), {alloc})

  Proof obligation:
    Case analysis on ctor variant (per Appendix A Forward Transfer
    Matrix, Construct row):
      Case ctor = Struct:
        TF-3 emits dst := (O, L, 1, u, bl, R<S>, {alloc});
        matches FRESH(R<S>).
      Case ctor = EnumVariant:
        TF-3 emits dst := (O, L, 1, u, bl, R<V>, {alloc});
        matches FRESH(R<V>).
      Case ctor in {ListLiteral, SetLiteral, MapLiteral}:
        TF-3 emits dst := (O, L, 1, u, bl, C, {alloc});
        matches FRESH(C).
      Case ctor in {Tuple, Closure}:
        TF-3 emits dst := (O, L, 1, u, bl, Phi, {alloc});
        matches FRESH(Phi).

    Monotonicity (L-6):
      TF-3 is a definitional rule; the post-state FRESH(shape) is
      the most-optimistic state in the product lattice for the
      Consumption x Cardinality x Uniqueness x Locality sub-lattice;
      composition with any subsequent transfer function preserves
      L-6 because the carrier is bottom (per per-dimension orderings).

    Lattice canonicalization:
      FRESH(shape) = (O, L, 1, u, bl, shape, {alloc});
      CN-1 vacuous (consumption=L != Dead, cardinality=1 != Absent);
      CN-3 vacuous (uniqueness=u, not Shared);
      CN-6 vacuous (locality=bl < HeapEscaping);
      CN-8 vacuous (access=O, not Borrowed);
      state is canonical at definition.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (per-ctor enumeration above)
      monotonicity (L-6 on TF-3's definitional post-state)
      lattice (canonicalization vacuity discharge)

